From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <datzeesix@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:54:07 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 50/85] Plutonium: several displays, a shell per display, one
 window in one place

EXO-DISPLAYS (docs/features/MULTI_MONITOR.md):

- PlutoniumShells opens every enabled shell's page on every display, each
  in a fullscreen app window there (display::ScopedDisplayForNewWindows),
  and keeps a visible shell per display. Pages on displays other than the
  startup one get "display=<id>" in their URL. "The visible shell" without
  a display is the focused display's (where the active window is); Show(),
  ShowNext() (Super+Tab) and the switcher act there. The shell last shown
  on each display is kept in local state (plutonium.display_shells) and
  shown again when the display comes back.
- Hotplug: a new display gets its shells' pages; an unplugged display's
  pages are hidden before Ash moves them, then closed. What they showed
  stays in the shared pool (the other shells' Elsewhere).
- Only the visible shell on each display drives what it shows
  (IsVisibleShell() is per display). A switch on one display takes only
  that shell's elements out of fullscreen, and its <embed>s don't take
  tabs another display's visible shell shows.
- One window, one place: a <native-window> attaching a window takes it
  from other pages' elements, which get NativeWindowClient.OnTaken() and
  fire "windowtaken" (windowState "taken"). A hidden shell's page doesn't
  take a window from a visible one; it gets it, as a page that lost one
  does, when its shell is shown, or once no page shows the window.
- The broker: getDisplays() and "displayschanged" (NativeDisplayEntry),
  displays and visibleOn on ShellEntry, showWindowOnDisplay(),
  showTabOnDisplay() (the visible shell there gets a focus request) and
  focusDisplay().
- Keys: Super+Shift+Left/Right focus the next display, with Ctrl too they
  move the focused window or tab there, unless the shell takes the keys.
- The switcher: "Show on display N" for windows, tabs and shells.
- DevTools: Plutonium.setDisplaysForTesting (with
  --plutonium-test-displays) replaces the displays, for hotplug on X11.
